    "lineEnd": 0,
    "lineStart": 0,
    "memoText": " \n                          VETO MESSAGE - No. 31\n \nTO THE SENATE:\n \nI am returning herewith, without my approval, the following bill:\n \nSenate Bill Number 7782-A, entitled:\n \n    \"AN ACT to amend the public health law, in relation to requiring the\n      department  of health to enter into a contract for the digitaliza-\n      tion and indexing of certain vital records\"\n \n    NOT APPROVED\n \n  This bill would require the Department  of  Health  to  enter  into  a\ncontract  for  the  digitalization  and  indexing of vital records at no\ndirect cost to the state.\n \n  I recognize the importance of the work of the Department  of  Health's\nBureau  of  Vital Records, as well as the burden of researching historic\nrecords that may be centuries old. However, legislation is not  required\nfor  the  Department of Health to update its systems of recordkeeping. I\nam directing the Department of Health to assess vendors that can  assist\nwith digitizing vital records to facilitate public access and streamline\ndepartmental processes.\n \n  Therefore, I am constrained to veto this bill.\n \n  The bill is disapproved.                       (signed) KATHY HOCHUL\n \n                               __________\n",
